 "review": {
  "score": 8.0,
  "round": 3,
  "problems": [
   "The four dark rocks at the base (rx 7\u201310, char1 fill with a steel stroke) look a lot like the tube openings. At a glance they could be read as more holes in the seabed rather than stones.",
   "The tubes are nearly straight cones. The spec asks for sponges that 'swell and gently bend', but the walls barely bulge, so the shape looks a little stiff next to branching coral.",
   "The two bubbles (y -162 and y -176) float about 10\u201325 px above the tallest tube with no visual link to it. That is fine underwater, but they are faint and close to clutter."
  ]
 },
 "for": "Cluster of hollow, finger-shaped yellow and orange tube sponges rising from the seabed. They add organic, rounded shapes that contrast with the branching coral.",
